WEBVTT

00:25.250 --> 00:32.210
<b>Beyond Journey's End</b>

01:29.990 --> 01:32.990
Episode 36: A Magnificent End

02:15.480 --> 02:18.750
<i>As I thought, this won't be easy.</i>

02:20.940 --> 02:25.000
<i>It's like fighting multiple 
master swordsmen at once.</i>

02:25.760 --> 02:27.780
<i>On top of the sheer number of attacks,</i>

02:27.780 --> 02:31.000
<i>his reflexes and stamina 
far exceed human levels.</i>

02:31.980 --> 02:34.080
<i>Stark is being overpowered.</i>

02:34.080 --> 02:37.990
<i>If this becomes a battle 
of endurance, we're sure to lose.</i>

02:38.960 --> 02:41.040
<i>Should we retreat and regroup?</i>

02:41.960 --> 02:46.420
<i>No, he's faster than us. 
He'd chase us down.</i>

02:47.910 --> 02:51.230
<i>This is bad. Frieren was right.</i>

02:51.230 --> 02:53.140
<i>I can't read his attacks.</i>

02:55.330 --> 02:56.570
<i>In that case...</i>

03:01.120 --> 03:04.120
<i>Fool. I told him not to 
take his attacks head-on.</i>

03:04.590 --> 03:05.630
You are mine.

03:08.110 --> 03:10.430
<i>He let himself get cut on purpose?</i>

03:10.430 --> 03:11.880
<i>He's one tough kid.</i>

03:18.240 --> 03:21.870
Stark, you're a skilled warrior.

03:21.870 --> 03:24.510
You created the slight opening I needed.

03:34.040 --> 03:36.110
It's over, Revolte.

03:36.600 --> 03:38.860
Wait. I remember now.

03:40.110 --> 03:44.490
You're the partner of the 
first-class mage I killed before.

03:45.270 --> 03:48.370
I recall the situation 
was similar to this one.

03:48.370 --> 03:54.250
You'd gone off to slay other demons, 
while your partner defended the village.

03:54.830 --> 04:00.080
By the time you returned, it was too late.

04:00.480 --> 04:03.580
Don't you want to know 
how your partner died?

04:03.580 --> 04:04.580
Silence.

04:05.140 --> 04:09.600
I learned a truly interesting 
lesson from that battle.

04:09.600 --> 04:12.690
Enough. I'll silence you myself.

04:14.040 --> 04:18.110
Then I have one last 
piece of advice for you.

04:18.540 --> 04:22.830
You should check more 
thoroughly for survivors.

04:24.380 --> 04:25.430
A child?

04:32.360 --> 04:33.830
You're just delaying the inevitable.

04:47.110 --> 04:50.820
I did it! I did it, Lord Revolte!

04:50.820 --> 04:51.650
Praise—

04:57.360 --> 04:59.860
Well done. You have my thanks.

05:00.710 --> 05:02.740
<i>My judgment was clouded.</i>

05:03.080 --> 05:05.840
<i>For a moment, 
all I could think of was him.</i>

05:06.240 --> 05:10.560
<i>I knew there couldn't be a child here.</i>

05:12.670 --> 05:19.130
I was right. Humans have a habit 
of protecting their young.

05:21.270 --> 05:23.030
Do we?

05:23.030 --> 05:28.970
If that were true, the world 
would be a more peaceful place.

05:29.560 --> 05:36.130
I only ever knew one idiot who died 
protecting a child he didn't know.

05:39.610 --> 05:43.610
Perhaps he was too kind.

05:44.050 --> 05:45.850
It's the same in every era.

05:46.710 --> 05:49.620
Kind mages don't live long.

05:50.020 --> 05:52.130
He met a magnificent end.

05:54.950 --> 05:57.360
So even you say things you don't mean.

05:57.970 --> 06:00.990
Genau, you're an unpleasant man.

06:01.440 --> 06:03.290
You don't have a shred of kindness.

06:08.300 --> 06:10.040
Stay that way forever.

06:13.410 --> 06:14.900
As you wish.

06:16.230 --> 06:20.260
I do not enjoy killing.

06:20.700 --> 06:22.480
I shall put you out of your misery.

06:24.420 --> 06:28.230
I shouldn't have acted out of character.

06:37.250 --> 06:38.750
I'm surprised.

06:39.280 --> 06:45.800
I didn't think there was a warrior alive 
who could stop a direct hit from me.

06:46.500 --> 06:51.250
You can still move? 
You should've played dead.

06:51.750 --> 06:53.910
Then we would've lost.

06:55.380 --> 07:00.520
Battles are won by whoever's 
still standing at the end!

07:01.210 --> 07:05.700
I thought you were a good person, 
but you're just an idiot.

07:06.400 --> 07:08.740
That's not a bad philosophy, though.

07:11.240 --> 07:14.830
I shall walk into the jaws 
of death with you, Stark.

07:15.180 --> 07:20.590
The more desperate the battle, the more 
catharsis you feel when you survive.

07:20.970 --> 07:25.080
I'm looking forward to that. 
I can't stop shaking.

07:38.990 --> 07:40.140
<i>What should I do?</i>

07:43.750 --> 07:47.030
<i>Ms. Frieren disappeared at some point.</i>

07:51.660 --> 07:55.800
It's nice to watch from afar 
once in a while.

08:09.760 --> 08:12.670
It's pointless trying 
to conceal your mana and hide.

08:14.130 --> 08:17.850
I created this fog with magic.

08:17.850 --> 08:21.770
It can detect and identify targets 
from the faintest traces of mana.

08:22.760 --> 08:26.980
No living creature can 
conceal their mana completely.

08:35.860 --> 08:39.450
<i>Visibility is poor, 
and he's blocking my attacks.</i>

08:40.020 --> 08:41.520
<i>It's a bad matchup.</i>

08:57.830 --> 09:01.720
<i>I sense that Ms. Fern 
is struggling as well.</i>

09:02.210 --> 09:03.790
<i>It's understandable.</i>

09:03.790 --> 09:07.480
<i>Her opponent seems to be a demon 
who uses unconventional magic.</i>

09:07.760 --> 09:08.980
Medrozobalt.

09:13.280 --> 09:17.030
What are you looking at? 
I am your opponent.

09:17.030 --> 09:18.740
I know.

09:29.420 --> 09:32.820
<i>Meanwhile, my opponent is the
 opposite of "unconventional."</i>

09:32.820 --> 09:36.090
<i>Her combat style is tried-and-tested.</i>

09:36.090 --> 09:39.840
<i>Defending even while she attacks.
 Her fundamentals are solid.</i>

09:40.210 --> 09:41.760
<i>She simply has no openings.</i>

09:42.660 --> 09:46.180
<i>I mustn't face her head-on.</i>

09:51.390 --> 09:56.150
<i>Ideally, I'd work with Ms. Fern 
to bring both down,</i>

09:56.590 --> 10:00.910
<i>but this fog likely has powerful 
mana-detection capabilities.</i>

10:01.520 --> 10:06.370
<i>Currently, Ms. Fern can't use stealth, 
her greatest asset.</i>

10:06.370 --> 10:12.380
<i>In which case, the situation would change 
greatly if this magic fog were removed.</i>

10:13.530 --> 10:15.250
Shall I cut loose a little?

10:26.590 --> 10:27.790
<i>A flurry of blows?</i>

10:27.790 --> 10:29.650
<i>Her attack pattern changed!</i>

10:49.600 --> 10:53.620
I recognize this fighting style.

10:53.970 --> 10:58.690
It's similar to one used by a clan that 
hunted demons on the Northern Plateau.

10:59.730 --> 11:04.520
An insane clan that dedicated 
their lives to killing demons.

11:05.120 --> 11:06.900
How interesting.

11:07.760 --> 11:09.940
This should be a good match.

11:11.040 --> 11:13.150
Let's have a fair fight.

11:21.430 --> 11:24.570
<i>He's fast. I can't land any of my spells.</i>

11:26.790 --> 11:32.880
<i>His masterful movements have become 
those of a savage predator.</i>

11:38.780 --> 11:42.520
<i>He's still fighting despite the 
life-threatening wounds he's suffered.</i>

11:42.990 --> 11:47.710
<i>He has superhuman toughness 
and inexhaustible stamina.</i>

11:48.020 --> 11:51.680
<i>At this rate, he really will 
kill us through attrition.</i>

12:47.100 --> 12:49.950
Genau, his swords have weakened!

12:49.950 --> 12:51.320
We can break them!

12:51.320 --> 12:57.460
Indeed, he doesn't have the focus to 
maintain the mana in his swords anymore.

12:57.960 --> 12:59.390
Three to go!

13:04.930 --> 13:06.090
<i>Wait.</i>

13:06.390 --> 13:08.100
<i>Why does something feel off?</i>

13:09.300 --> 13:13.850
<i>Her attacks are ferocious, 
but I sense no bloodlust.</i>

13:14.330 --> 13:17.230
Oh, you really are astute.

13:18.270 --> 13:21.860
But it took you too long to notice.

13:21.860 --> 13:24.360
I've just finished analyzing the fog.

13:27.280 --> 13:32.620
Those who only know how to fight 
only learn spells for combat.

13:32.940 --> 13:38.380
Any other member of my clan probably 
wouldn't have made it out of here.

13:39.040 --> 13:43.250
Because I doubt they'd 
know how fun magic is.

13:47.530 --> 13:49.300
Erilfrachte.

13:56.590 --> 13:58.400
<i>The fog cleared.</i>

13:58.980 --> 14:00.390
<i>How pointless.</i>

14:01.540 --> 14:04.010
<i>I can simply create it again.</i>

14:09.010 --> 14:11.190
Where did that girl go?

14:22.910 --> 14:24.970
<i>Hemmung's mana vanished.</i>

14:39.100 --> 14:41.810
<i>An attack? From where?</i>

14:55.270 --> 14:56.540
Zoltraak.

15:00.970 --> 15:02.300
She's so far—

15:12.050 --> 15:15.530
A super-long-range attack from 
outside their detection radius

15:15.530 --> 15:17.230
whose trajectory can't be predicted.

15:18.010 --> 15:20.600
Not bad, Fern. I'm impressed.

15:22.870 --> 15:25.860
I'd rather not fight a battle 
this difficult again.

15:36.490 --> 15:37.540
Two to go!

15:40.270 --> 15:41.290
One!

15:51.110 --> 15:53.180
It's over, Revolte.

16:01.020 --> 16:05.680
Only humans think empty hands 
can't be weapons on their own.

16:06.150 --> 16:10.690
Your fatal assumption was that I wouldn't 
be able to fight if you disarmed me.

16:11.220 --> 16:13.000
I win.

16:14.180 --> 16:19.460
<i>Our</i> fatal assumption? I think you'll find 
both humans and demons make those.

16:19.940 --> 16:23.070
For instance, you don't know 
how tenacious humans can be.

16:35.850 --> 16:37.590
Cleaving Light!

16:43.630 --> 16:45.150
Digardnacht.

17:03.950 --> 17:07.400
You seem like a good person to me, too.

17:08.610 --> 17:12.140
You're still trying to defend the village,
even after it's been destroyed.

17:13.340 --> 17:15.510
I couldn't do that.

17:29.760 --> 17:32.730
You're still trying to save me.

17:37.400 --> 17:39.070
I knew it.

17:39.870 --> 17:42.330
You're a good guy after all.

18:15.890 --> 18:17.450
Methode.

18:18.340 --> 18:21.370
Did I fail to die again?

18:21.370 --> 18:23.110
It would seem that way.

18:23.710 --> 18:25.730
Enough. I can move again.

18:30.350 --> 18:31.630
How is Stark?

18:31.630 --> 18:35.260
It was a close call, but he'll survive.

18:37.480 --> 18:40.750
I prioritized healing him over you.

18:52.790 --> 18:54.020
I see.

18:54.280 --> 18:56.020
Does that displease you?

18:56.020 --> 18:59.780
No. He did well.

19:00.880 --> 19:05.400
Ms. Frieren's party will be staying 
in the village for a while.

19:24.050 --> 19:27.550
Seems like I'm mostly better.

19:27.870 --> 19:29.500
He's doing push-ups.

19:29.500 --> 19:33.060
Could Mr. Stark possibly 
be a freak of nature?

19:33.560 --> 19:34.610
That's so mean.

19:35.040 --> 19:38.950
I noticed your party 
doesn't have a priest.

19:39.320 --> 19:43.750
I'll be free for a while 
once this job is over.

19:43.750 --> 19:45.710
Shall I accompany you?

19:47.040 --> 19:50.820
The Northern Plateau is dangerous 
without priest spells.

19:51.200 --> 19:52.770
We'll be fine.

19:52.770 --> 19:56.330
I can't cast anything high-level 
like healing magic,

19:56.330 --> 19:59.380
but I know a few priest spells.

20:00.400 --> 20:03.860
If we find ourselves in serious trouble, 
we can always run away.

20:03.860 --> 20:05.720
That's what we've done until now.

20:06.890 --> 20:11.100
Besides, we want to keep 
our priest slot open.

20:12.680 --> 20:15.260
We might see him again someday.

20:16.000 --> 20:17.160
And...

20:18.030 --> 20:21.490
For some reason, Fern seems 
unhappy when you're around.

20:21.980 --> 20:24.980
Oh, my. I've made her hate me.

20:25.380 --> 20:28.770
But I also love you, Ms. Fern.

20:28.770 --> 20:31.120
You're so cute when you're angry.

20:32.090 --> 20:33.000
Methode.

20:33.480 --> 20:35.620
The Chivalric Order of Norm have arrived.

20:35.990 --> 20:39.970
We'll be accompanying 
them back to the south.

20:40.750 --> 20:42.340
Understood.

20:42.860 --> 20:45.430
This is where we say goodbye.

20:47.130 --> 20:49.630
Stark, how are your injuries?

20:51.070 --> 20:53.260
All good. No problem.

20:53.520 --> 20:54.480
I see.

20:55.350 --> 20:57.830
I owe you all a debt.

20:57.830 --> 20:59.720
One I intend to repay someday.

21:00.280 --> 21:01.420
Mr. Genau.

21:03.590 --> 21:04.900
You're forgetting something.

21:08.040 --> 21:10.410
Thank you for your help.

21:11.380 --> 21:13.110
No, thank you.

21:13.110 --> 21:14.910
I hope both of us live long lives.

21:17.380 --> 21:18.520
Let's go.

21:18.520 --> 21:19.420
Yes, sir.

21:20.150 --> 21:21.280
See you later.

21:21.890 --> 21:22.680
Yeah.

21:23.160 --> 21:24.680
May our paths cross again.

21:53.770 --> 21:56.700
Was it really the right move 
to turn her down?

21:58.460 --> 22:00.150
Methode, I mean.

22:00.980 --> 22:03.710
This party's priest is Sein.

22:03.710 --> 22:07.390
No, I mean she's a pretty older lady.

22:07.390 --> 22:10.220
Won't Sein complain 
when we see him again?

22:10.830 --> 22:15.850
Who cares? This party 
already has an older lady.

22:17.150 --> 22:18.860
I guess that's true.

